From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 19:12:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: apple: t8132-j604: say the dcpext routes carry DP
 Alt Mode

The comment on the dcpext Type-C routes had them carry DisplayPort
tunnels only, as on the J713. The J604 device tree describes a DP PHY on
each Type-C ATC (atc0/1/3-dpphy, "atc-dpphy,t8132", not tunnelled), and
the PHY and display drivers now run DP Alt Mode on its four lanes with
the calibration the boot loader copies. Say so. Comment only: the
compiled tree does not change.

[j604: X2-01 C3 (BOARD-SWEEP-1838 row X2).]

Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5.5
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604-dcpext.dtsi | 11 +++++++----
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604-dcpext.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604-dcpext.dtsi
index a20e980a09..07e045e566 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604-dcpext.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604-dcpext.dtsi
@@ -204,10 +204,13 @@
  * dcpext0's Type-C routes: the three USB-C ports (ATC0, ATC1, ATC3), UFP
  * mux selector 2 on each ATC crossbar (cells 0/1/2: DP PHY, DP IN0, DP IN1;
  * the J604 device tree names the same cells as dp-switch-dfp-port 0/1/2 and
- * the ATC as dp-switch-dfp-endpoint 0/1/3). As on the J713 the routes are
- * for DisplayPort tunnels and stay disabled; they are enabled only for a
- * dcpext the boot loader handed over, since a USB-C port controller waits
- * for every available route. Route N uses the names typecN.
+ * the ATC as dp-switch-dfp-endpoint 0/1/3). The routes carry DisplayPort
+ * tunnels and DP Alt Mode: the J604 device tree has a DP PHY on each of these
+ * ATCs (atc0/1/3-dpphy, not tunnelled), which runs four DP lanes (pin
+ * assignments C and E) with the calibration the boot loader copies. They
+ * stay disabled here and are enabled only for a dcpext the boot loader
+ * handed over, since a USB-C port controller waits for every available
+ * route. Route N uses the names typecN.
  */
 &dcpext0 {
 	apple,connector-type = "USB-C";
